    "answer": "**Tesla, Inc. – Annual Cash‑Flow Statement (Last 4 Fiscal Years)**  \n_Source: OpenBB / FMP (structured statement)_\n\n| Fiscal Year | Period Ending | Net Cash from Operating Activities | Net Cash from Investing Activities | Net Cash from Financing Activities | Net Change in Cash & Equivalents | Cash at Beginning of Period | Cash at End of Period |\n|-------------|---------------|-------------------------------------|------------------------------------|------------------------------------|----------------------------------|-----------------------------|-----------------------|\n| **2025** | 2025‑12‑31 | **$14,747 M** | **$(15,478 M)** | **$1,139 M** | **$579 M** | $17,037 M | $17,616 M |\n| **2024** | 2024‑12‑31 | **$14,923 M** | **$(18,787 M)** | **$3,853 M** | **$(152 M)** | $17,189 M | $17,037 M |\n| **2023** | 2023‑12‑31 | **$13,256 M** | **$(15,584 M)** | **$2,589 M** | **$265 M** | $16,924 M | $17,189 M |\n| **2022** | 2022‑12‑31 | **$14,724 M** | **$(11,973 M)** | **$(3,527 M)** | **$(1,220 M)** | $18,144 M | $16,924 M |\n\n**Key Highlights**\n\n- Tesla’s operating cash flow has remained strong, ranging from $13.3 B (2023) to $14.9 B (2024).\n- Investing cash outflows have been significant, largely due to capital expenditures and investment purchases.\n- Financing activities have varied, with 2024 showing a net inflow of $3.9 B, while 2022 had a net outflow of $3.5 B.\n- Net change in cash has been positive in 2025, 2023, and 2022, but slightly negative in 2024.\n\nThese figures are taken directly from the structured cash‑flow statement retrieved via the `get_financial_statement_tool`.",
